WEBVTT

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:17.620
After overcoming many obstacles,
the Ionodai skate-leading team

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.370
finally became one because of me,
the brilliant Hayato Sasugai.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.950
Some people might have a different opinion,
but I know it was thanks to me.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.370
Now, it's a matter of seeing how much
they can surpass their past selves.

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.500
They'll need to keep their cool to do so,

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.410
but there's one guy who's bad at that...

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.700
"Keyaki Park Ice Arena"

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.700
but there's one guy who's bad at that...

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.660
"Day before 4th competition"

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.660
All right! One more time!

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.450
Not "one more time."

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.790
Tomorrow's the fourth competition of the series.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.330
Don't get too excited right now.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.200
I can't sit still.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.660
If I don't move my body, I'll be like "Ahh!"

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.910
Use those feelings in the competition.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:08.160
Make sure you rest your body
enough in order to do that.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.000
I can't sleep.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.830
You have to.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:11.700
Immerse yourself completely in lukewarm water.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.580
When you get out, stretch and massage your body.
Get rid of the lactic acid buildup.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.080
If you're gonna eat, eat something
with a lot of vitamin B1 or B2.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.330
But don't eat too much.
You won't be able to digest it all.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:20.330
Also--

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:23.870
So you <i>can</i> sleep.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.500
...four-six... toad oil...

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.290
...that's an octopus...

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.080
I have my schedule, and a map.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.200
Jonouchi gets motion sickness,
so I have medicine for that.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.040
Aki sometimes gets a fever,
so I have some cooling sheets.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.830
Oh, right. I should bring two extra cards.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.580
Are you sure you're using enough toner?

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.000
It's fine.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.950
It's important to take care of your
skin properly while you're young.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.700
I don't care about stuff like that.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.870
Sota, dear?

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.200
Sota, how much longer are you
going to play your video game?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.330
I can't sleep, so what choice do I have?!

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.330
Oh, dear! I'm going to tell your grandmother.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:26.790
Tomorrow, huh?

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.290
"College Entrance Exams"

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.290
Tomorrow, huh?

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:40.870
It's finally here, huh?
The day we face off directly.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.160
Oh? Everyone from Ionodai, all together.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.450
"Episode 8
Champions"

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:24.540
The fourth competition of the Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series--

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:27.450
All the teams have already
finished their short programs,

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.370
and we are now at the intermission.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.620
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.620
Here are the results of the short program:

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.410
"1. St. Clavis Gakuin High School
2. Ionodai High School"

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.410
In first place is St. Clavis Gakuin.

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.790
With their overwhelming strength,
they held on to the top spot this time, too.

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.450
Next, in second is last year's
fourth place winner, Ionodai High.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.620
With their carefree performance,
they got their best score ever.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:48.330
They're closing in on the
first-place team, St. Clavis Gakuin.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.540
There's a big point difference
between them and the next schools,

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.330
Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei and Kusano Mukaibara.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.700
--Ms. Abe--
--Yes?

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:00.660
Only the free skate is left, but
what do you think will happen next?

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.790
Well, I expect all the schools
will fight hard until the end,

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:10.200
but in this case, I think it's safe to say
that St. Clavis Gakuin and Ionodai High

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.200
will be the top two finishers
of the fourth competition.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.870
You've got a smug look on your face,

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.160
but aren't you forgetting to thank the
person who carried you home last night?

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.290
My right knee still hurts, you know.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:21.870
Sorry about that!

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.200
Izumi,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.870
the match between your old teammates
and Shinozaki's team has already started.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.410
You can watch it if you'd like.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.870
I'm fine.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.370
I can just watch the recording later.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.790
You're so indifferent.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.160
Himekawa!

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.410
You don't have to be so cold.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.660
There's jewelry that's polished by emotion.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.120
Don't you agree?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.160
Number Two Prince?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.950
Kuonji? From Yokohama?

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.450
Is he real?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.250
I was in the area on location for a TV show,

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.910
so I thought I'd pay a courtesy visit.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.450
Did he make an appointment?

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:00.910
No, I don't know...

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:04.620
Come, Himekawa. Let's go watch this
match between Maeshima and Shinozaki,

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:08.410
which can be written as "destiny"
and read as "opening act."

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.330
There's a nice Japanese café nearby.
I'll take you there.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.160
There's a lot I want to talk
about with you, too.

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.200
--Wait, why should I--

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.910
--That sounds good.
--Wait, why should I--

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:19.750
Go with him. You're too tense right now.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.700
You should have him teach
you how to relax a little.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.000
No, please wait. I can't accept
that this guy from Yokohama--

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.580
If you just go home,

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.040
I'll take you off the starting roster
for the next competition.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:31.750
It looks like you've got permission.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:33.950
Come on, let's go, "Princess River."

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.580
Don't call me that.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.910
They are currently smoothing
the ice for the free skate.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:54.830
So, let's look back at St. Clavis Gakuin
and Ionodai High's short programs.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.160
First, what's your impression
of the two schools, Ms. Abe?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:58.790
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:58.790
I'm sure St. Clavis needs no explanation.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.330
I'm sure St. Clavis needs no explanation.

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.870
They've been called an unbeatable powerhouse,

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.160
and as such, they're steady and reliable.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:11.040
Shinozaki competed in singles before,
but he's better at teamwork than expected,

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.950
so they have a team of very strong skaters.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:18.790
They're one or two steps above
the other high schools.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.080
But like in their previous competition,

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.910
the entertainment aspect seems
to be difficult for Shinozaki,

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.370
and they did not gain
as many points as expected.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.080
It was still a pretty high score, though.

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:31.080
What about Ionodai High School?

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.330
Compared to their performance in the
first competition, they feel more stable.

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.750
They've added this wild edginess
and have grown in an interesting way.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.660
--However, their score dropped considerably
in the free skate last time...

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.200
--Why are you streaming this?
--However, their score dropped considerably
in the free skate last time...

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.790
You can just watch the live broadcast
on the TV in the lobby.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:53.580
Very well.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:56.500
I'll tell you when the top-ranking teams skate.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.790
He could tell with just that?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.620
As expected of their father.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.950
Pretty good pics, right?

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:10.410
Keep it up, and tell everyone else, too.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.580
Got it.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:13.370
Eat now, while you can.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.080
The free skate is a lot longer
than the short program.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.120
Okay.

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.080
Second, huh? Not a bad start.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.200
"Skate Rink Map for Competitors and Staff"
        "Main Rink"

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.200
"Practice Rink"

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.370
"Skate Rink Map for Competitors and Staff"
        "Main Rink"
                                                     "Practice Rink"

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:24.370
Right now, the three teams going first

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.290
are in the bottom rink
for their six-minute practice.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:30.500
Ours will start after that, but...

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.120
Where's Maeshima?

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.160
--Dunno...
--You idiot!

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.370
He was dancing around the
basement levels, so I brought him here.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.450
Doing this to your costume
before the performance!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.450
Hurry up and take it off! And then sit down!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.250
I wonder what's going on over there.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.500
Could there be trouble?

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.830
Tomo, help me!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:46.660
Right!

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.540
What are you doing?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.830
Will you be able to skate properly like that?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.620
There's no time left before the performance.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.410
I'm resting already.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:55.450
Tomo, hair dryer.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.500
Okay.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.500
I'm asking if you feel any
remorse for what you did.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:00.290
Kiriyama.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:02.870
Maeshima, what were you doing?

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.080
Practicing.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:06.450
You should limit yourself.
If you do it like that--

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:08.450
I'm sorry.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:12.620
But, if you don't give it your all,
can you say you're skating seriously?

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.870
I just want to push myself
as close to my limit as I can.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.200
I had that break from skating, too.
I am sorry for causing Yuki trouble, though.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.910
It's fine. Just be quiet.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.950
Our strategy is as I told you
in our meeting yesterday.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.410
You remember the changes to the routine, right?

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.250
Yes, sir.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.790
So that's the unruly horse
everyone's talking about?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.040
He's just as the rumors say.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:33.700
Throwing the team into disorder
like that right before the performance.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.750
It's fine, isn't it?

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:38.580
Everyone has their own way
of getting and staying motivated.

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:43.290
Besides, the way you're talking could
lead you to underestimate your opponent.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.120
Don't be distracted by outside forces.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.290
Yes, sir!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.000
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.700
We will now begin the free skate
of the fourth competition

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:56.200
of the Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.040
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.410
"Fukushima
Kusano Mukaibara High School"

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:01.410
Skating first is Kusano Mukaibara
High School of Fukushima.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.040
"Japanese I"

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.040
"Anmitsu"

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:15.660
And now... a triple Lutz.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.950
This I's desserts are really sweet
and good despite being low in calories.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.870
Athletes can eat without worrying here.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.750
I always make them let me come
when I'm in the area.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:29.410
Thanks for always coming here, Noa.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.870
I also always look forward
to seeing your face, ma'am.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.580
Oh, my.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.660
I thought we were here to watch the competition.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.120
Of course we'll watch!

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:40.160
But I wanted to talk to you.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.580
Conversations over food
close emotional distance.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.790
Food?

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:46.790
What will you have?

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.830
I recommend the <i>anmitsu</i> set here.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:49.660
Water.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.000
Two <i>anmitsu</i> sets, please!

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.410
Coming right up!

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.700
By the way, what's your favorite food?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:55.540
Water.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.540
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.000
"Champions"

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.000
"Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix"

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.080
"Clam Rice"

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.910
"Clam Rice"

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.910
Um, one of these clam rice bentos, please.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:06.200
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:06.910
"Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei High School"

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.830
"Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei High School"

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.830
We're now in the second half of the free skate.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.450
"Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei High School"

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.450
Kanazawa Nishiizumi Kogei did their best,

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.330
but they didn't get as
many points as they'd hoped.

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:15.250
They're currently fourth overall.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.540
Oh, their mistakes in the
second half cost them, huh?

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.250
There are two schools left.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:23.120
The next performance will
be by Ionodai High School,

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.040
who placed second in the short program.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:31.160
"Ionodai High School"

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.080
Very nice. They're very together!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.500
They're showing us the same stability
they had during the short program.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.000
But it starts from here, doesn't it?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.330
That's true.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:19.080
It's no small feat to keep up with
Maeshima's dynamic movements.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.160
It's true that it's no small feat...

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.910
It doesn't show in their faces,

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:30.200
but it looks like they're doing
all they can just to keep up?

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.450
On the other hand, that unruly horse's
emotions are showing too much.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.500
"I want to win. I want to win."

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.700
It's true that bare emotions can
give momentum to a performance.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:42.160
It's easier for the judges to award points
with this positive attitude, too.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.580
But one wrong step, and it'll go out of control.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.950
If he doesn't learn how to control his emotions,

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.000
it'll end up being the same
as the first competition.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.660
It'll end with their downfall.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.410
Emotional control? What's that?

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:03.450
That guy's not that good of a student.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:06.000
I'm not really one to talk,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.410
but Maeshima's working hard
because he wants to win.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:10.750
At least understand that much.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.450
Also, instead of making Maeshima go smaller,

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:16.290
you should let him skate with all his emotions.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.290
Yeah. We'll back him up.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:20.580
No, you don't have to.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.370
If you're thinking about backing him up,
your movements will get smaller.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.580
Rather, you should get carried along with him.

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.620
You came to make Himuro
taste bitter defeat, right?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.370
It's a good chance.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.910
Well, we'll at least hear you out.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:40.200
Everyone should already have the technique
needed to keep up with Maeshima.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.120
Right, Coach?

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.830
Yeah, that's what I taught you.

00:13:44.830 --> 00:13:46.790
But...

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:48.910
Please, Vice-Captain.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.330
If you can cling onto Maeshima,
the whole performance will look grander,

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.620
and it'll appeal to the judges.

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:56.660
It'll make it easier for the wing
and guards to skate, too.

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.120
Easier said than done.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.620
I believe in you.

00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:01.290
Don't say things you're not used to.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.410
Have I ever lied to you at a time like this?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.620
Jonouchi, sir!

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:09.370
Didn't get enough sleep 'cause
you were gaming too much?

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:11.160
That's not true...!

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.910
I could tell by watching the short program.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:14.160
But it's an opportunity.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.620
They say people perform better
when they're a little tired.

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.160
Really?

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:23.120
Wouldn't it be cool to say
"I removed my limiter"?

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:26.500
I can use that.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.540
I just said it 'cause it sounds good, though.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.450
What is it?

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.450
Do your best.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.910
At what?

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:36.200
Go.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.910
Seize the victory with your
whole bodies and souls.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.160
That's this team's style!

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:43.250
I'll win!

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.040
--Win!
--I'm so cool!

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:50.290
They did it!

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:51.870
All five of them landed it cleanly!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:52.750
--Magnificent! It's so wild
and heroic and powerful!

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:55.000
--This is my first time seeing this...
--Magnificent! It's so wild
and heroic and powerful!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:58.330
Me, too. They're shouting with
their whole bodies that they'll win.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.080
Sho and the others are so cool!

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:03.040
Stop getting all excited, you guys.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.950
If you do that, then I'll want to win, too!

00:15:06.950 --> 00:15:10.910
Skate-leading performances are
sometimes called "group dancing,"

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.950
but this really is the very
definition of a boisterous dance!

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:22.040
They did it!

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:23.500
They really did it!

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:27.370
Ionodai High didn't let the results
of the first competition haunt them

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.450
and gave a wonderful performance that
showed what amazing skaters they are!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:41.700
"Ionodai High School"

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.910
"Ionodai High School"

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:42.910
There they are!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.500
"Ionodai High School"

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.500
With a total score of 138.48,

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.620
"1. Ionodai High School"

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.620
With a total score of 138.48,

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.750
"1. Ionodai High School"

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.750
they've got the highest scores
in this competition!

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.200
"1. Ionodai High School"

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.200
They've shot to the top!

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.910
It must be because they
didn't make any mistakes,

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.660
each skater got the points he could,
and they got high scores for their artistry!

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:59.910
I think even St. Clavis will have
a hard time beating this score.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.080
Shinozaki! Well, did you see us?

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:04.950
We definitely won!

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.910
You haven't changed at all.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.410
I'll tell you one more time.

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:09.620
Huh?

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.540
No matter how much you think you've progressed,

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.000
you will never be able to beat me.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:17.160
No, you're actually regressing.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.330
Hey, what are you doing?

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.870
Stop it, Maeshima!

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:23.870
You little... Always looking down on me!

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:26.540
Aren't his actions problematic?

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:29.500
Sorry about this. Apologize, Maeshima.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.660
There's no need to apologize, is there?

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:34.250
You guys insulted us first.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:39.290
Besides, if we got suspended, <i>you</i> would
be disappointed, too, wouldn't you?

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:43.000
Mr. Shinozaki.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.160
Don't worry. We'll compete
against you fair and square.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.080
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.660
Captain, we're going with <i>that</i> plan, right?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.250
Yeah. I'm counting on you two.

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.450
Leave it to us.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.950
"St. Clavis Gakuin High School
Gallant Figure"

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.910
It's finally time for the last performance
of the fourth competition in this series.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:13.000
What kind of performance
will the favorite to win show us?

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.750
Oh?

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.120
The piece they're using is different,

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:27.580
but it's the exact same choreography as Ionodai!

00:17:27.580 --> 00:17:32.250
Shinozaki's their only lead,
but they've changed their routine!

00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:36.870
Is this a coincidence--

00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:38.370
Of course not.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.950
To be able to do this much last minute...

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.580
In contrast to Ionodai,
who used their agility and power,

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.080
St. Clavis's performance is so fluid!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:49.250
It looks like they've gone back
to their original routine here.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:54.790
That Shinozaki looks quiet,
but he's actually really competitive...

00:17:54.790 --> 00:17:57.830
Change the routine?

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:00.950
Just the beginning.
To the same as what Ionodai High had.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:02.620
Why do you want to do that...?

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.660
Did they set you off?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.660
With your abilities, you can handle it.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:11.830
One of our later elements
will come at the beginning,

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.000
so we'll have to make adjustments
to the second half of the program, too.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:17.000
I mean, we probably <i>can</i> do it, but...

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:18.750
Got it. Let's do it.

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:19.700
Captain?!

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.870
It's fine.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.580
As I'm sure you guys have seen, too,

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:26.750
Ionodai will probably keep getting high scores.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.040
If we leave them alone,
they might become a nuisance.

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:33.250
That's why we'll crush them now.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.620
We'll make sure they know who the champions are.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:38.790
You can do it, right, Shinozaki?

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:44.200
I was surprised at first when he suggested it,

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.790
but it means that's how much
Shinozaki is aware of Maeshima.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:50.620
It's true that Ionodai performed well.

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:52.540
But we can't lose.

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.500
Our goal is to win twice consecutively.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:58.200
To not let anyone else to the top.
A complete victory!

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.580
We have a better foundation.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:02.750
We've accumulated the practice hours.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:06.200
We're much more polished than you guys,
with your raw materials laid bare.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:09.500
We'll show you who's the real protagonist!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.250
Watch...

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.540
Watch...!

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.750
Watch me!

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:26.330
Did Shinozaki just land a quadruple Axel?!

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:29.290
This is what a champion looks like!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:39.870
They did it! They really did it!

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:43.540
No mistakes? St. Clavis had
a performance with no mistakes!

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:47.160
All I can say is "Wow." It was really amazing!

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:50.870
Have they scored higher
than Ionodai High School?

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.700
Oh? Where are you going?

00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:03.080
To practice.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.540
You're not going to wait for the results?

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:08.160
I don't care about the results.
I'll pay you back later.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.200
You're impatient, aren't you?

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:11.950
Ma'am, check please.

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:13.200
Okay.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:19.580
I won't let those guys
be the only ones fired up, damn it!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.790
It's true. Practice makes perfect.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.160
"13th Boys' High School
Skate-Leading Grand Prix Series"

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.160
Now, here are their scores!

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.870
"St. Clavis Gakuin High School"

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.870
Now, here are their scores!

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.910
"St. Clavis Gakuin High School"

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:32.910
Their total is 139.65!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:37.080
Their score was even higher
than Ionodai's best score of the series,

00:20:37.080 --> 00:20:40.000
and with that, they win first place
at the fourth competition!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:41.620
St. Clavis Gakuin!

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:45.540
It's amazing. I've never seen such
a high-level competition before!

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:49.580
With this, St. Clavis has two
consecutive wins in this series,

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.330
and have stayed on top for every
competition they've skated in so far!

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:58.120
A solid record to take them on their way
to two consecutive wins at nationals!

00:21:01.120 --> 00:21:03.080
"Grand Prix 4th Competition Results
1. St. Clavis Gakuin High School
2. Ionodai High School
3. Kusano Mukaibara High School"

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.950
This is all part of your calculations... right?

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:11.160
Yeah. Actually, it's even
higher than I predicted.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.370
It'll all come down to the Grand Prix finals.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.000
Maeshima.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:18.580
I acknowledge your persistence
to win and your hard work.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:20.790
So...

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:22.700
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:25.370
Yes, sir.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.790
I've grasped it. That feeling.

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.040
The way that felt--

00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:39.200
Yeah, at the very least,
it felt better than last year.

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:45.700
Those are the future possibilities
that your hard work has brought.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.500
Then...

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:51.370
We can do it! We can go even further!

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:37.040
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.160
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.160
I'm Michinaga from St. Clavis!
And this guy's Yamashita.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:43.540
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:43.540
--Yup.
--We're older than Shinozaki,
but it's hard to talk to him.

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:46.000
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:46.000
--Yeah.
--But Kurayoshi helps us out.

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:46.910
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:46.910
Yeah!

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:48.910
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:48.910
Yamashita, you really okay
just taking it easy like that?

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:50.620
"Next time" "Two People"

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:50.620
Don't get so serious all of a sudden.
